CHAPTER.VERS:
But we are persuaded of you

          {+}
        , beloved, better things that follow salvation, though we thus speak:

for God is not unrighteous to forget your

          {+}
         work and the love which you

          {+}
         showed toward his name, in that you

          {+}
         served the saints, and still do serve.

And we desire that each of you

          {+}
         may show the same diligence to the fullness of hope even to the end:

that you

          {+}
         are not sluggish, but imitators of them who through faith and patience inherit the promises.
